":450,"estimated_tokens_delta":50,"uuid":"83390c26-fd2b-4a2b-b78b-6509c1403eba","session_id":"ec13c223-2ae3-41a1-871e-6a1869e10bfc"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcysNtZfB3WdWzHRuSwDN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5284,"cache_read_input_tokens":18515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5284},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec13c223-2ae3-41a1-871e-6a1869e10bfc","uuid":"1f49a1f7-3546-45bb-a884-55ac9388cc56","request_id":"req_011CcysNs5MmmqVioC4B6DE9"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CcysNtZfB3WdWzHRuSwDN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## JWT auth plan (Node/Express)\n\n**Setup**\n- Add deps: `jsonwebtoken`, `bcrypt` (password hashing), and a validator (`zod` or `express-validator`).\n- Store `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET`, `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET`, and TTLs in env (never hardcode). Fail fast on boot if missing.\n\n**Core pieces**\n- **User store**: users table/collection with a `passwordHash` (bcrypt, cost ~12). Registration hashes; login compares.\n- **Token service**: `signAccess` (~15 min) and `signRefresh` (~7 days), plus verify helpers. Keep signing/verifying in one module so config lives in one place.\n- **Auth routes**: `POST /register`, `POST /login` (issues both tokens), `POST /refresh` (rotates and reissues), `POST /logout` (revokes refresh token).\n- **Auth middleware**: reads `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, verifies the access token, attaches `req.user`, returns 401 on failure. Apply to protected routes.\n\n**Hardening (do these, not optional)**\n- Generic error messages on login (don't reveal which field was wrong); rate-limit `/login` and `/refresh`.\n- Refresh-token rotation + a revocation store (denylist or per-user token version) so logout/compromise actually invalidates.\n\n**Two decisions that change the code — pick before I start:**\n1. **Token transport**: `Authorization` header (simplest, good for pure APIs/mobile) vs **httpOnly cookies** (safer against XSS but needs CSRF protection). Default I'd take: header for an API, unless a browser SPA shares the origin.\n2. **Refresh strategy**: stateless access-only (simplest, but no server-side logout) vs access+refresh with a revocation store (what I outlined above). Default: access+refresh.\n\nTell me your stack specifics — DB (Postgres/Mongo/other), TS or JS, and SPA vs mobile/third-party client — and I'll tailor the plan and then implement.\n\nWant me to proceed with the defaults above?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5284,"cache_read_input_tokens":18515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5284},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ec13c223-2ae3-41a1-871e-6a1869e10bfc","uuid":"04ba2e1f-ca16-4755-bccb-4d0f04e6fe03","request_id":"req_011CcysNs5MmmqVioC4B6DE9"},{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":19805,"duration_api_ms":20776,"ttft_ms":9579,"ttft_stream_ms":2039,"time_to_request_ms":440,"num_turns":1,"result":"## JWT auth plan (Node/Express)\n\n**Setup**\n- Add deps: `jsonwebtoken`, `bcrypt` (password hashing), and a validator (`zod` or `express-validator`).\n- Store `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET`, `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET`, and TTLs in env (never hardcode). Fail fast on boot if missing.\n\n**Core pieces**\n- **User store**: users table/collection with a `passwordHash` (bcrypt, cost ~12). Registration hashes; login compares.\n- **Token service**: `signAccess` (~15 min) and `signRefresh` (~7 days), plus verify helpers. Keep signing/verifying in one module so config lives in one place.\n- **Auth routes**: `POST /register`, `POST /login` (issues both tokens), `POST /refresh` (rotates and reissues), `POST /logout` (revokes refresh token).\n- **Auth middleware**: reads `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, verifies the access token, attaches `req.user`, returns 401 on failure. Apply to protected routes.\n\n**Hardening (do these, not optional)**\n- Generic error messages on login (don't reveal which field was wrong); rate-limit `/login` and `/refresh`.\n- Refresh-token rotation + a revocation store (denylist or per-user token version) so logout/compromise actually invalidates.\n\n**Two decisions that change the code — pick before I start:**\n1. **Token transport**: `Authorization` header (simplest, good for pure APIs/mobile) vs **httpOnly cookies** (safer against XSS but needs CSRF protection). Default I'd take: header for an API, unless a browser SPA shares the origin.\n2. **Refresh strategy**: stateless access-only (simplest, but no server-side logout) vs access+refresh with a revocation store (what I outlined above). Default: access+refresh.\n\nTell me your stack specifics — DB (Postgres/Mongo/other), TS or JS, and SPA vs mobile/third-party client — and I'll tailor the plan and then implement.\n\nWant me to proceed with the defaults above?","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ec13c223-2ae3-41a1-871e-6a1869e10bfc","total_cost_usd":0.0933025,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5284,"cache_read_input_tokens":18515,"output_tokens":1223,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5284,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1223,"cache_read_input_tokens":18515,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5284,"cache_creation":{"